  <prompt>
    Add a dual-deploy warning section to `.claude/skills/code-page-deploy/SKILL.md` explaining the pattern (code-page A's vite.config.ts aliasing another code-page B's source tree causes dual-deploy trap). Add a companion note to `docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md`. Cite the LegalWorkspace ← SpaarkeAi pair as historical example (now resolved by FR-10 as of task 022).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE docs contributor + skill-directives maintainer.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `code-page-deploy` SKILL.md has a new "Dual-deploy warning" section. Widget-authoring guide has a companion note. Future contributors are alerted to the pattern.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The dual-deploy trap: code page A's vite.config.ts aliases code page B's source (e.g., `@spaarke/legal-workspace/src` → `../LegalWorkspace/src`). Deploying B alone does NOT propagate changes to A (A keeps its bundled snapshot from A's last build). This trapped ~30 min of debug time during 2026-07-01 UAT. FR-10 (task 022) resolved the specific SpaarkeAi ← LegalWorkspace case; FR-09 documents the pattern for future contributors so they don't rediscover it the hard way.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>.claude/skills/code-page-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§3">Touches `.claude/` — MUST be sequential (main-session-only). Sub-agent write boundary applies.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Keep warning concise: paragraph + short recipe (grep target's vite.config for resolve.alias to sibling src trees).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Note the historical LegalWorkspace ← SpaarkeAi case as resolved (post-FR-10) so future readers know it was closed.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2/spec.md</file>
