      <file>docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read spec.md § FR-09. Read `code-page-deploy` SKILL.md to identify a good insertion point (recommend near the "Deploy" step or a new "Known traps" section).</step>
    <step order="2">Add a section to SKILL.md titled "Dual-deploy warning (aliased-source pairs)": paragraph explains the pattern; recipe: `grep -r "resolve.alias" src/solutions/*/vite.config.ts` to enumerate pairs; check the target's aliases + rebuild any aliased sibling. Cite historical LegalWorkspace ← SpaarkeAi case as RESOLVED by R2's FR-10.</step>
    <step order="3">Add companion note to `docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md` (find a fitting section — recommend § 12 or new § "Deployment considerations"). One paragraph pointing to the skill's warning section.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify no other consumers of the doc/skill break. Grep for `code-page-deploy` in other skills — if any depends on section ordering, don't break.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: 025 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Edit files; grep</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="skill">.claude/skills/code-page-deploy/SKILL.md (modified — new warning section)</output>
    <output type="docs">docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md (modified — companion note)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep on SKILL.md finds new "Dual-deploy" section.</criterion>
